<div class="guide">

  <section class="guide-chapter">
    <h2 class="chapter-head"><span class="mono chapter-num">§01</span> Conversation format</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li><span class="mono timeline-num">1</span> Introduction <span class="mono timeline-time">2&ndash;3 min</span></li>
      <li><span class="mono timeline-num">2</span> Your background <span class="mono timeline-time">5&ndash;7 min</span></li>
      <li><span class="mono timeline-num">3</span> Main discussion <span class="mono timeline-time">30&ndash;40 min</span></li>
      <li><span class="mono timeline-num">4</span> Closing thoughts <span class="mono timeline-time">5 min</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-chapter">
    <h2 class="chapter-head"><span class="mono chapter-num">§02</span> Pre-interview questionnaire</h2>
    <p>Please share the following information at least 3 days before our scheduled conversation.</p>

    <h3 class="group-title">About you</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>How you&rsquo;d like to be introduced (brief bio)</li>
      <li>Name pronunciation and professional title</li>
      <li>Relevant links (website, social media, projects)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="group-title">Conversation topics</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>2&ndash;3 main topics you&rsquo;d like to discuss</li>
      <li>Any specific questions you&rsquo;d like us to ask</li>
      <li>Topics you&rsquo;d prefer not to discuss</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="group-title">For our audience</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Key takeaways you hope listeners will gain</li>
      <li>Any resources or recommendations to share</li>
      <li>Call-to-action for listeners (if applicable)</li>
    </ul>

    <p>When you&rsquo;re ready, submit your answers using <a class="inline-link" href="/guest-pre-interview/">this form</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-chapter">
    <h2 class="chapter-head"><span class="mono chapter-num">§03</span> Day of interview checklist</h2>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Test your audio and video setup</li>
      <li>Close unnecessary applications</li>
      <li>Silence notifications</li>
      <li>Restart your computer (helps prevent technical issues)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-chapter">
    <h2 class="chapter-head"><span class="mono chapter-num">§04</span> Technical setup guide</h2>

    <h3 class="group-title">Interview platform</h3>
    <p>We use Riverside.fm for remote interviews. It provides high-quality audio and video recording with separate tracks for host and guest. Simple browser-based interface, no downloads required.</p>

    <h3 class="group-title">Audio equipment</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Apple microphones (including MacBook built-in) work well</li>
      <li>External mics like Blue Yeti or Audio-Technica are great</li>
      <li>Position microphone 6&ndash;8 inches from your mouth</li>
      <li>Use wired headphones to prevent echo</li>
      <li>Find a quiet environment with minimal background noise</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="group-title">Video &amp; environment</h3>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Position camera at eye level (external webcam preferred)</li>
      <li>Face a light source; avoid being backlit</li>
      <li>Choose a clean, uncluttered background</li>
      <li>Use a wired internet connection when possible</li>
      <li>Find a quiet space with minimal echo</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="guide-signoff">We&rsquo;re looking forward to a great discussion!</p>
</div>
